  "knowledge_gaps": [
    "The matched-mask control isolates context removal, but both arms discard supervision relative to the corrected baseline. Include an unmodified baseline to establish whether cropping improves the original training procedure.",
    "Padding-safe recurrence is assumed rather than specified. Zero embeddings can still change GRU hidden states through biases. Define hidden-state initialization, padding handling, aligned output reconstruction, and empty-history behavior consistently in training and the embedded predictor.",
    "A dedicated crop generator alone does not guarantee matched experiments. Specify reproducible batch, negative-sampling, crop-plan, and dropout streams; define the exact loss mask, loss normalization, checkpoint rule, and handling of short histories.",
    "Uniform cropping by event count does not directly test age-based staleness. Its effects depend on history truncation and interaction frequency, and full-history inference introduces a training–inference context mismatch.",
    "The report lacks a budget allocation and a precise validation selection protocol. Compare complete four-category configurations using macro HR@10, quantify paired uncertainty where host outputs permit, and avoid interpreting a single-seed result as seed robustness.",
    "Originality 5/10 and difficulty 3/10 are insufficiently justified without closer augmentation comparisons and verification of the supplied GRU implementation. Potential 7/10 remains speculative; no measured context-removal or validation improvement is available."
  ],
  "follow_up_queries": [
    {
      "reason": "Clarify novelty and determine whether a simpler recency intervention deserves comparison before assigning originality and potential ratings.",
      "query": "Sequential recommendation GRU4Rec stochastic prefix cropping suffix subsequence augmentation matched next-item targets: how do methods such as Recency Sampling and sequence-cropping augmentation differ in retained supervision, persistent-preference loss, and full-history inference mismatch?"
    },
    {
      "reason": "Resolve the main implementation ambiguity that could invalidate the context comparison or break predictor consistency.",
      "query": "PyTorch GRU left-padded variable-length sequences: why do zero padding embeddings still update hidden states, and how can valid events be compacted, packed with pack_padded_sequence, and mapped back to aligned next-item loss positions while preserving final nonpadding readout?"
    },
    {
      "reason": "Strengthen the experimental design so improvements can be attributed to context removal and assessed under the fixed search budget.",
      "query": "Controlled ablation design for stochastic sequence cropping in recommendation: compare unchanged baseline, full-context matched-loss-mask control, and cropped-context training; separate random streams for sampling and dropout; assess paired HR@10 uncertainty and repeated validation selection bias with one fixed training seed and 200 users per dataset."
    }
  ]
